{
  "id": "valid-sudoku",
  "questionId": "valid-sudoku",
  "slug": "valid-sudoku",
  "title": "Valid Sudoku",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Hash map",
  "patterns": [
    "hashing",
    "matrix validation"
  ],
  "lists": [
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "you need to check three different kinds of groups (rows, columns, boxes) for duplicates - can you check all three at once in a single pass over the cells?",
    "for each cell, what row index, column index, and box index does it belong to? the box index can be computed from (row / 3) * 3 + (col / 3)",
    "keep 9 sets for rows, 9 for columns, and 9 for boxes; when you visit a non-zero cell, check if its value is already in the corresponding three sets before adding it",
    "skip cells that are 0 (empty), they never cause a conflict",
    "return false the moment you find a value already present in its row, column, or box set - no need to keep scanning"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "treating 0 as a real digit that can conflict with other 0s (empty cells should always be skipped)",
    "computing the wrong box index, e.g. using row * 3 + col instead of (row / 3) * 3 + (col / 3) with integer division",
    "checking rows and columns but forgetting to also check the 3x3 boxes, or vice versa",
    "using floating point division for the box index instead of integer division, which shifts cells into the wrong box"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a 9x9 grid `board` representing a partially filled Sudoku board. Each cell holds a digit from 1 to 9, or 0 to mark an empty cell (the original puzzle uses a blank square, but since inputs here are integers only, 0 stands in for \"empty\").\n\n**Determine whether the board, as filled in so far, obeys Sudoku's placement rules: each row must not contain the same digit twice, each column must not contain the same digit twice, and each of the nine non-overlapping 3x3 sub-boxes must not contain the same digit twice.**\n\nEmpty cells are ignored entirely, and the board does not need to be completely filled or solvable, only currently consistent with these rules.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "board.length == 9",
      "board[i].length == 9 for every row",
      "0 <= board[i][j] <= 9, where 0 means empty"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "a completely empty (all-zero) board, which is always valid",
      "a completely filled, fully valid 9x9 solution",
      "two equal digits in the same 3x3 box but different rows and columns",
      "two equal digits in the same row or column but different (and not overlapping) 3x3 boxes"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "board = [[5,3,0,0,7,0,0,0,0],[6,0,0,1,9,5,0,0,0],[0,9,8,0,0,0,0,6,0],[8,0,0,0,6,0,0,0,3],[4,0,0,8,0,3,0,0,1],[7,0,0,0,2,0,0,0,6],[0,6,0,0,0,0,2,8,0],[0,0,0,4,1,9,0,0,5],[0,0,0,0,8,0,0,7,9]]",
        "output": "true",
        "expectedOutput": "true",
        "explanation": "no row, column, or 3x3 box has a repeated non-zero digit"
      },
      {
